  "$comment": "Pins the single-hop reading of a `jti` on a delegation token (#176 item 11, one-way door; see the draft PR). The token is otherwise del-001, validly signed by B, so the extra claim is the only defect under test. The `jti` is a valid UUID v4 in the RFC-AITP-0005 §2.2 layout, so its form is not under test.",
  "description": "Same token as del-001, except that the delegation claims carry a `jti` and no `chain`. RFC-AITP-0011 §1.1 says `jti` is not part of the single-hop claim set and that verifiers not opted into RFC-AITP-0011 reject `jti`-bearing tokens under the strict-claims rule. Receivers MUST reject with UNKNOWN_FIELD.",
